WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.730
"Fast X" has a cast full of A-list action
stars, but we nearly got an appearance from

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.570
"John Wick" himself.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.000
Here's who Keanu Reeves would have played.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.210
One of the most impressive accomplishments
of the "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise is how it

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:18.238
managed to get some serious acting talent
to appear on-screen.

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:23.850
The most recent entry alone has numerous Oscar
winners among the cast, including Dame Helen

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.117
Mirren, Brie Larson, Charlize Theron, and
Rita Moreno.

00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:32.989
That's on top of casting rising talent in
Jason Momoa and Daniela Melchior.

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:38.553
However, if things had worked out differently,
another major star could have been on the roster.

00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:44.020
Alan Ritchson, who stars as scene-stealer
Aimes in "Fast X," revealed to Entertainment

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.886
Weekly that Keanu Reeves was initially courted
to play his part.

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:52.510
Reeves is no stranger to action-adventure
films, being the star of multiple franchises

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.420
like "The Matrix" and "John Wick."

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.379
Ritchson admitted it was tough to try to fill
those shoes:

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:01.980
"I was working on a movie with Hilary Swank
up in Winnipeg in the freezing cold, and I

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.740
got a call that things had shifted in the
plans with Keanu Reeves, which is I think

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.071
who was originally intended to play my part.

00:01:09.071 --> 00:01:10.397
Tough act to follow."

00:01:10.397 --> 00:01:15.725
Reeves may not be joining the "Fast" family
just yet, but it was a great opportunity for Ritchson.

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:20.992
Of course, it wasn't that easy, even without
having to compete with the star of "Point Break."

00:01:20.992 --> 00:01:25.320
Ritchson mentioned that there were "timing
issues" that could've necessitated another

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.743
recasting of Aimes.

00:01:26.743 --> 00:01:28.105
He went on to say,

00:01:28.105 --> 00:01:33.160
"Basically the deal was if there's no problems,
we don't shut down for COVID or weather, this

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.560
should work, and about two weeks later, we
got news that we were going to get hit with

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.799
the biggest blizzard in Winnipeg's history."

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:44.469
The production had to shut down temporarily,
and while Ritchson's "Fast" journey could've

00:01:44.469 --> 00:01:48.710
ended before it began, the production team
was able to move things around so that he

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.320
could be in the movie.

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:52.229
"Everyone becomes family.

00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:54.810
It's like a cult with cars."

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.900
However, that wasn't the end of Ritchson's
turmoil, as he recounted a phone call from

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.210
"Fast X" producer Jeff Kirschenbaum.

00:02:01.557 --> 00:02:02.777
He elaborated,

00:02:02.777 --> 00:02:04.659
"I was like, 'Oh, God.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:06.939
Whatever you've got to say, just say it.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:07.823
I can take it.

00:02:07.823 --> 00:02:08.823
I'm a big boy.'

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:13.370
He goes, 'You're not going to be working with
[director] Justin [Lin] on this.'

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.450
I was like, 'Okay ... am I still in the movie?'"

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.300
Kirschenbaum then clarified that Justin Lin
was the one who stepped away from the movie,

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.170
but Ritchson would still be in it.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.900
After that confusing back-and-forth, everything
was good, and Ritchson is now a proud member

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.370
of the "Fast" family.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.230
Meanwhile, Keanu Reeves certainly isn't short
on work, and he's had plenty of near-miss

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.403
appearances in franchise history.

00:02:36.403 --> 00:02:41.120
For example, he could've been part of the
Marvel Cinematic Universe in "Captain Marvel"

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.640
when he was offered the part of Yon-Rogg,
which ultimately went to Jude Law.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.890
He turned that down so that he could film
"John Wick: Chapter 3 — Parabellum."

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.220
And he could've had a very different role
in the "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise had another

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.227
opportunity worked out earlier.

00:02:56.227 --> 00:03:01.270
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
"Fast &amp; Furious Presents: Hobbs &amp; Shaw" director

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.740
David Leitch revealed that there were talks
early on for Reeves to play the part of the

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:09.220
Eteon director, who's nameless and faceless
in the film.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.510
However, as production went on, all parties
involved agreed that it just wasn't a good

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.290
fit, so Reeves passed.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:19.810
Still, there will be opportunities in the
future for Reeves to join the "Fast" franchise

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:20.810
if he wants.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.780
"Fast X" kicked off the beginning of the end
for the mainstay franchise, and it's been

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:31.280
confirmed that some spin-offs are in the works,
including one that will be female-led.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.790
It's safe to say that if Reeves really wants
to be part of the "Fast" family, any director

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.750
would jump at the chance to get him involved.

